{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds","id":1378370,"title":"Good DB builds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-03T15:26:25-07:00","id":1378370,"title":"Good DB builds","content":"So, with Heirs being somewhat available, what DB builds do people suggest? Any changes to your favorite combat set ups?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T15:48:25-07:00","id":1378380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds#post1378370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, with Heirs being somewhat available, what DB builds do people suggest? Any changes to your favorite combat set ups?</div> </div> </div> </div>IDK.<br /> <br /> If we say Deebs are &quot;Resonant&quot; with Shining Ice Mirror, then Air sword-fighter just got viable.<br /> <br /> Deeb archery just got insane.<br /> <br /> My ST literally cackled at the options this gives this arc's antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T15:55:49-07:00","id":1378384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1378380#post1378380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deeb archery just got insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? (Have only skimmed DB archery so far)<br /> <br /> Air-swordsman seems much more viable than before. I don't know if that makes it good, of course. With a quick read it seems to be about aiming and attacking people in metal armour?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T17:25:41-07:00","id":1378407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1378380#post1378380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IDK.<br /> <br /> If we say Deebs are &quot;Resonant&quot; with Shining Ice Mirror, then Air sword-fighter just got viable.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean if they get all the benefits which are listed for Solars in the core book (which would make sense, since Solars and DBs get the same benefits from Jade artifacts in the resonant/dissonant system)? What combos specifically with that weapon are you thinking of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T17:32:06-07:00","id":1378412,"title":"","content":"<b>Archery</b><br /> <br /> Rolling Stormcloud Approach breaks the archery-movement game a bit. Now that Air Stealth Archer who starts the fight off at extreme range and rains arrows down gets way more turns of free shots, basically she shoots you until she runs out of initiative, which considering she can be launching withering attacks may be more limited by terrain or enemies taking cover than anything. Which got even better because dodge got two new air charms, one of which makes Hopping Firecracker Evasion an Air charm as well and helps escape combat by adding a disengage to the movement roll.<br /> <br /> Landslide Missile Attack for Earth archery also lets you do a kind of similar thing. It knocks a target back, and possibly even down if they fall onto an earthen surface. With that you can aim at somebody at medium range, they move to Short, you fire and knock them back and down, they get up, you aim, they move to Short, fire again and knock them back and down. On its own it's not so great because you're only hitting for 1 damage each time, but combined with ranged allies it's great teamwork.<br /> <br /> <b>Awareness</b><br /> <br /> A bit of a teamwork enhancement here, with Victory-Seeking Insight you can now shift initiative around and even, potentially, generate a lot of it. If a party of 5 who all have this charm activate it they can each pay 4i to give their hearthmates initiative, and get 8i in return from all of them. Or even everyone dump everything they have into their hearthmate to give, say, a Fire Dragon stylist the guaranteed first turn with an epic decisive attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Brawl</b><br /> <br /> Water based Brawl can now strike AND grapple with Strength for really cheap, so that's good. If you want to be a super beefy brawler but low on Dexterity you only need to sacrifice defense. Also they can now clash, and losing the clash counts that as an onslaught penalty for yourself and allies. So like, Mela's Flashing Tongue where you make a number of withering attacks equal to their onslaught penalty, finishing off with a decisive one? That can be a good combo.<br /> <br /> <b>Dodge</b><br /> <br /> For dodge, apart from Air, now Water and Earth have more options. One benefits Earth aspected archers quite a bit as it's a charm that creates cover where there was none, or creates lots where there was some.<br /> <br /> The Heart like Water dodge charm that triggers on any successful decisive dodge, and lets you sent the attack back at the attacker with all the charms they enhanced it with, plus any Water Dragon charms, plus it doesn't reset you to base it resets them. Note that Flow With Strife, the water signature charm, lets you cancel levels of damage with initiative and cancelling all damage lets you count as dodging the attack. So you might take a big decisive hit, use some charms to lower the decisive damage, cancel the rest with Flow With Strife, and then smack the attacker with what they just hit you with.<br /> <br /> Also the games first reflexive rise from prone, which counteracts a lot of stuff. Air Dragon stylists like this.<br /> <br /> <b>Lore</b><br /> <br /> Mantle of Elemental Power lets you use Elemental Bolt attack as a Thrown or Archery weapon. You can use it with Persistant Hornet to make a living lightning bolt that harasses your enemies, you can use it to rain lightning from the skies with Arrow Rain Tempest, you can use Swallows Defend the Nest to pluck enemy arrows out of the sky with razor sharp thorns, and on top of all that it reduces the cost of EBA, and gives you an EBA based parry that even has +1 as though it were a medium weapon, and gives it additional range. Fuck. Yeah. This is what you take when you want to use elemental fury as your primary attack and defense.<br /> <br /> Also As in the Beginning, a charm so powerful I'm kind of torn on if it's too powerful. It doesn't deal any damage directly, has a huge cost, huge setup time, massive cooldown, bit penalty to using it...but combined with a full circle it wipes a city off the map. Anyone not killed instantly, in other words non-trivial characters, trying to fight the DB circle in the midst of that elemental hellstorm of fire, wind, lightning and poison is going to have a really bad time.<br /> <br /> <b>Melee</b><br /> <br /> Air swordsmen got like, a dozen new charms in melee. A whole new branch dedicated to aiming in melee. First you can aim and convert initiative to motes, then when you attack benefitting from aiming you reroll (Essence + enemy's mobility penalty) non-1 dice, with an upgrade that lets you reflexively aim before an attack. SO get this, you're wielding artifact twinblades at Essence 5, with a 16 die base attack, and you delay your action to clash, you clash with the enemy using Crossfire Flash, reflexive Unerring Lightning Razor, a full excellency and a level 2 stunt. You now have an effective 39 die attack, assuming none of your allies helpfully increased their mobility penalty to make it even more.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Scale Shield has so many different effects it's hard to say what's best, but the fact that Water can block an attack while under full defense and give the enemy an onslaught penalty in response is pretty good, especially combined with Water Dragon constantly benefiting from it.<br /> <br /> Earth also became pretty good protectors, at least against elemental or magical effects. Facing off against things like other Dragonblooded, or elemental gods, or just elementals lets them act as a grounding rod, pulling attacks away from their allies and buffing themselves with essence regeneration for the effort.<br /> <br /> <b>Resistance</b><br /> <br /> Dragon Graced Raiment is just fucking cool. Air based medium armor with no dodge penalty means medium armor has a real use now, and the fact that you can make epic elemental clothing out of it is great. The other effects are all useful, but don't, from what I see, change much, except maybe water ninja with concealable tag on any kind of armor. Apocalypse Outlasting Prana though, it's the first DB charm that lets them survive uncountable damage, and combined with Perfected Scales of the Dragon lets you survive seriously powerful decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Sail</b><br /> <br /> Earth aspects treat the deck of their ship as an earthen solid ground. Now Earth aspected captains get to use all their fancy mountain strength charms while naval fighting. Some other charms give DBs a bit of an edge in naval combat, including broadsides with ships lacking anti-ship weaponry and momentum dice tricks. Having a DB captain saddle up beside your ship in a racing schooner and then blow a hole in it with fire essence would be quite the surprise.<br /> <br /> <b>Thrown</b><br /> <br /> Sand Scourge Feint is a new distract charm, Earth based, and it lets you steal initiative from the guy you're distracting and give it to your ally, with initiative break if applicable, by expending your aura rather than paying the cost.<br /> <br /> <b>War</b><br /> <br /> Even more teamwork charms, this time dual-combo attack charms. Especially when combined with that new awareness charm it could get really powerful, like you start the fight, the person with lower initiative dumps 5i into the guy with higher, making for +6i with the free one, then they act first and combo strike with the same high initiative, preemptive onslaught penalties. Or, even better, use its upgrade charm on turn 2 after distract gambiting for even MORE initiative, getting full free excellencies and actually being able to combine multiple elements together even if they're aura keyworded.<br /> <br /> That's pretty good. Now, at Essence 5 (I know, I know no game ever in the history of Exalted has gotten to Essence 5) that combined with With One Mind, which is a charm that when you're benefiting from a distract gambit from an ally, your attack has double 7s on the attack roll. Technically you don't even need to benefit from it, just as long as it was attempted.<br /> <br /> I think with that the real question is what combo builds can TWO players make, that will destroy anything. It's on a cooldown, once per story unless you overcome a major obstacle by protecting a hearthmate, or working together to defeat a powerful foe, so it's not something you use every fight, but it's really cool.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T01:38:06-07:00","id":1378486,"title":"","content":"Nice summary, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T04:02:34-07:00","id":1378498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1378486#post1378486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice summary, thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much seconded.<br /> <br /> My guess is, like DrLoveMonkey says, Victory-Seeking Insight and Tiger-and-Dragon Combination are the things that will have the most immediate impact on typical games as they're available from standard chargen and they address one of DBs' major problems \u2013 having enough initiative to threaten real top-top-tier opponents. With the former, a spec'd up hearth of DBs is going to have the option for big alpha strikes, while with the latter your defensive buddy who has been relentlessly defend-othering you while you poke for initiative is suddenly potentially deadly.<br /> <br /> Having a suitable DB retainer is suddenly even more useful than ever. Cue Fire swordsman 'Initiative Parasite' and his faithful Earth squire 'Finishing Move'.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Feel like the dodge tree got a big boost. If you're using it, you're going to want to take Safety Among Enemies as one of your signature charms now to get Heart Like Water if it stays as it is.<br /> <br /> Air looks like the stand-out winner of Dragon-Graced Rainment as you say, in fact Air seems to have gotten a lot more combat oomph in general \u2013 medium armour-wearing air melee-ist aims, uses Flying Dagger Leap to make an unencumbered rush and unleashes the new air combat tree in all its glory...<br /> <br /> That's just the personal scale stuff too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-04-2020, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T05:12:47-07:00","id":1378505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1378384#post1378384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? (Have only skimmed DB archery so far)<br /> <br /> Air-swordsman seems much more viable than before. I don't know if that makes it good, of course. With a quick read it seems to be about aiming and attacking people in metal armour?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rolling Stormcloud Approach. Aim at Long range, your opponent moves to medium, you fire and move back to Long, your opponent moves to Medium, you move back to Long and Aim. Repeat.<br /> <br /> You fire every other turn, meaning even with a full Excellency, you gain 1m a turn whilst kiting.<br /> <br /> You can use those motes on Ice-Slick Tread Technique. Now not only do you stay at Long range, but you leave difficult terrain behind you.<br /> <br /> Line of Sight a problem? With Skyward Eye Vigil you only need line of effect.<br /> <br /> Nimble Zephyr Defense means you gain Init when foes miss you. Light-as-Clouds Method and Heart Like Water for if you foe can catch you.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Graced Raiment hands you significant defensive advantages. And it combos well with Blood-Chilling Strike which just stops your foe moving.<br /> <br /> So it goes something like this:<br /> <br /> I get a bonus success on my Stealth roll. I launch an unexpected attack from Medium range, which stops you moving, even with Charms, then move back to Long (leaving a rangeband of difficult terrain between us). If you are an Archer who can somehow Reflexively Aim at me, then I turn your attack with all its Charms right back at you. If you are not an Archer, you do nothing whilst I aim at you, regenerating motes. Unless you can One More Step + Thunderbolt Attack Prana me, you will never catch me as I fill the area with difficult terrain, Aiming and moving. And if you do catch me, you better not let me Dodge or else I'm moving out to Medium with a Reflexive Disengage that fills the area between us with more difficult terrain.<br /> <br /> Then there's Tiger-And-Dragon...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1378407#post1378407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean if they get all the benefits which are listed for Solars in the core book (which would make sense, since Solars and DBs get the same benefits from Jade artifacts in the resonant/dissonant system)? What combos specifically with that weapon are you thinking of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every time you Aim with Shining Ice mirror, you gain +2 non-Charm defense.<br /> <br /> Cold Moon Slash lets you attack from Medium if you Aimed.<br /> <br /> Long range.<br /> Turn 1: Aim. Get +2 Defense, +3 to hit.<br /> Enemy moves to Medium.<br /> Turn 2: Attack out to Medium range, inflicting mobility penalties (Cold Moon Slash) and reroll (Essence+mobility penalty) failures on attack and damage roll (Unerring Lightning Razor). Wound Penalties on foe.<br /> Enemy moves to Short.<br /> Turn 3: Steel Tempest Strike allows a free Reflexive attack. Ice Fixing Strike Stacks a -1 Defense. Then your actual turn. Unerring Lightning Razor with Willpower for the extra +2 non-Charm defense, +3 Accuracy and reroll (Essence+mobility penalty) failures on attack and damage roll (remembering the increased penalty from Cold Moon Slash). Winter Night Cut for another -1 Defense and -2 on attacks.<br /> Enemy attacks you (at -2, -Wound Penalties, at +2 Defense).<br /> Turn 4: Unerring Lightning Razor + Fulminating Thunderclap Surge gives you an Unblockable, -4 (-2 Defense, -2 Mobility, -? Wound) Evasion, attack with +3 dice to hit and damage, reroll (Essence+mobility penalty) failures on attack and damage roll.<br /> <br /> There is no Turn 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-04-2020, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T06:32:26-07:00","id":1378520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1378505#post1378505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every time you Aim with Shining Ice mirror, you gain +2 non-Charm defense.<br /> <br /> Cold Moon Slash lets you attack from Medium if you Aimed.<br /> <br /> Long range.<br /> Turn 1: Aim. Get +2 Defense, +3 to hit.<br /> Enemy moves to Medium.<br /> Turn 2: Attack out to Medium range, inflicting mobility penalties and reroll (Essence+mobility penalty) failures on attack and damage roll (Unerring Lightning Razor). Wound Penalties on foe.<br /> Enemy moves to Short.<br /> Turn 3: Steel Tempest Strike allows a free Reflexive attack. Ice Fixing Strike Stacks a -1 Defense. Then your actual turn. Unerring Lightning Razor with Willpower for the extra +2 non-Charm defense and reroll (Essence+mobility penalty) failures on attack and damage roll (remembering the increased penalty from Cold Moon Slash). Winter Night Cut for another -1 Defense and -2 on attacks.<br /> Enemy attacks you (at -2, -Wound Penalties, at +2 Defense).<br /> Turn 4: Unerring Lightning Razor + Fulminating Thunderclap Surge gives you an Unblockable, -4 (-2 Defense, -2 Mobility, -? Wound) Evasion, attack with +3 dice to hit and damage, reroll (Essence+mobility penalty) failures on attack and damage roll.<br /> <br /> There is no Turn 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just, that's... well, it's awesome.<br /> <br /> Soooo... Shining Ice Mirror = Relentless Wind? (Arada's sword from 2e, no idea if still canon).<br /> <br /> How viable is air-melee is without the artefact do you reckon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-04-2020, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T07:59:23-07:00","id":1378544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1378520#post1378520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How viable is air-melee is <b>without the artefact</b> do you reckon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing the game as intended against published antagonists: Air Melee has gone from &quot;awkward and weak&quot; to &quot;solidly playable&quot;.<br /> <br /> Combat Optimized: Air Melee has gone from &quot;unplayable&quot; to &quot;suboptimal&quot;. It hits a good niche if your Kinship can pile Onslaught onto a single target (e.g. if you are paired with a Fire Immaculate or Steel Devil) but still needs help with crowd control (Thousandfold Tempest Strike is E4 but fills a massive gaping hole in Terrestrial offense). Fire Melee and Water Dragon Shining Into the Void are stronger builds. Mounted Wood Switch Hitter is also clearly better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-04-2020, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T09:48:51-07:00","id":1378569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1378412#post1378412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Archery</b><br /> Also the games first reflexive rise from prone, which counteracts a lot of stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars had one first.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mantle of Elemental Power lets you use Elemental Bolt attack as a Thrown or Archery weapon. </div> </div> </div>But you could <i>already</i> do that?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sand Scourge Feint is a new distract charm, Earth based, and it lets you steal initiative from the guy you're distracting and give it to your ally, with initiative break if applicable, by expending your aura rather than paying the cost. </div> </div> </div>In retrospect, &quot;Pocket Sand!&quot; was an obvious hole in the Dragon-Blooded Thrown Charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T10:13:47-07:00","id":1378573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1378569#post1378569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars had one first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn that\u2019s what I get for not being well versed in Lunars<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1378569#post1378569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you could <i>already</i> do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite, EBA is a simple charm, so if you wanted to use Swallows Defend the Nest or Persistent Hornet Attack with it you\u2019re out of luck. You could shoot stuff with it, yes, but you couldn\u2019t do all the things you could with an archery or thrown weapon. Plus with that up it only costs one more to use which is a lot more friendly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T10:39:05-07:00","id":1378581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1378573#post1378573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite, EBA is a simple charm</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, right. I forgot that and the conflicts that would arise from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T02:52:03-07:00","id":1378958,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d be really interested to see if anyone has already come up with any builds using the new charms from Heirs (or even just general DB ideas they really wanna try out or found work for them), so to get the ball rolling here\u2019s one that ruthlessly rips off the work of others as a starter for 10. It\u2019s (by my standards) min-maxed. I\u2019d probably tone it down some for play (your mileage may vary etc).<br /> <br /> Haven\u2019t included merits or specialties, but the basic concept is\u2026<br /> <br /> <b><u>Chargen Dynast Ambush Archer</u></b><br /> <br /> Based heavily on DrLoveMonkey\u2019s build here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1344771%23post1344771\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1344771#post1344771</a><br /> <br /> And aspiring to play like the advice of JohnDoe244 earlier in this thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1378505%23post1378505\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1378505#post1378505</a><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Air Aspect</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">ATTRIBUTES</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">3 Strength<br /> 5 Dexterity<br /> 1 Stamina<br /> <br /> 1 Charisma<br /> 4 Manipulation<br /> 2 Appearance<br /> <br /> 5 Perception<br /> 1 Intelligence<br /> 5 Wits</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">ABILITIES (all BP used here)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Aspect</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Linguistics 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Lore 0</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Occult 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Stealth 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Thrown 0</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Favoured</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Awareness 5<br /> War 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Athletics 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Dodge 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Archery 5</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Other</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Integrity 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Resistance 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Socialise 3<br /> Survival 3</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">CHARMS</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Free Excellencies (5)<br /> Archery</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Athletics</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Awareness</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Dodge<br /> Stealth<br /> <br /> Archery (5)<br /> Harvest of the Hunter<br /> Sky-Calming Draw<br /> Arrow Thorn Technique<br /> Death From Nowhere<br /> Drawing Lightning Style</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Athletics (2)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Bellows-Pumping Stride</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Ice-Slick Tread Technique</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Dodge (4)</span><br /> Flickering Candle Meditation<br /> Nimble Zephyr Defense<br /> Hopping Firecracker Evasion<br /> Light-as-Clouds Method<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Resistance (1)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Ox-Body Technique</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Stealth (3)<br /> Soundless Action Prana<br /> Vanishing Wind-Body Technique</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Blood-Chilling Strike</span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Advancement (rough notes/intentions):<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> CHARMS:<br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Combat, combat, combat:</span></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Go to town on archery and awareness charms, prioritising Rolling Stormcloud Approach (<i>the absolute must have</i>) and Skyward Eye Vigil when available</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">More Ox-Bodies</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">At Essence 3, get Whispering Dragon Soul and Zone of Silence and </span>from Dodge get Elusive Crosswinds Defence, Safety Amongst Enemies and then Heart Like Water (at Essence 4)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Less of a priority, but getting some Athletics and Resistance up to Dragon-Graced Raiment would be useful</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Evocations depending on what merits you buy</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">--</span><br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Other (sort of):</span></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Grab the Integrity excellency</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Get some Occult to help handle spirits, maybe learning sorcery (the reason your Occult is at 3) to get Beckons That Which Stirs The Sky to play up your combat advantages in bad weather</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Buy up the Linguistics tree, prioritising the silent communication charms to coordinate ambushes</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Potentially get some Survival to help endure/hunt foes in the wilderness. A sneaky bird familiar might come in handy</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">--</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">NON-CHARMS:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The way you spent your bonus points you should be set for a while on skills, so I\u2019d shore up your slightly embarrassing attributes first of all. Stamina and Intelligence both to 3 would be my focus</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Would enjoy any critiques anyone has to share and definitely would love seeing anything anyone else has come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-24-2020, 05:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T06:26:14-07:00","id":1379470,"title":"","content":"Idle musings on other stuff from the PDF, based around (a subject I'm probably too hung up about) making effective-ish builds outside the usual aspect ability match-ups or just going with the default Immaculate style...<br /> <br /> 1. Earth-focused melee \u2013 I've previously figured 'why would you do this when Earth Dragon is <i>right there</i>?', but it looks a bit more of a thing now? Getting an artefact heavy weapon to get the full benefit of Dragon-Scale Shield, pair it with Dragon-Graced Weapon and your preferred heirloom Grand Goremaul/Stone of the Ram's Horn combo and you've got Earth Dragon lite without the merit expenditure and access to the very good melee tree.<br /> <br /> Throw in heavy armour, ISoS and spamming Ox-Bodies, maybe with some mundane throwing weapons and Sand-Sourge Feint for a bit of range/surprise factor and you'd maybe get a decent feel of an implacable Earthy warrior out of chargen that doesn't have to have been an Immaculate.<br /> <br /> Anyone with more experience got a feel for how good the magma charm is?<br /> <br /> 2. 5/1/5 Brawler \u2013 mucking around with trying to make this, well, not good but fun to play thanks to Flotsam-and-Jetsam Approach (FYI, basically allows you to use strength with improvised weapons for a scene for 1m). End up just spamming Ox-Bodies at the minute, and realising that Water has so many toys it's hard to justify going with any other aspect, even if I'd like to make an Ragara Earth-aspected brutish debt collector work (although honourable mention for Wood and Oaken Thew Exertion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T11:10:33-07:00","id":1379497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1379470#post1379470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Earth-focused melee \u2013 I've previously figured 'why would you do this when Earth Dragon is <i>right there</i>?', but it looks a bit more of a thing now? Getting an artefact heavy weapon to get the full benefit of Dragon-Scale Shield, pair it with Dragon-Graced Weapon and your preferred heirloom Grand Goremaul/Stone of the Ram's Horn combo and you've got Earth Dragon lite without the merit expenditure and access to the very good melee tree.<br /> <br /> Anyone with more experience got a feel for how good the magma charm is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Earth-melee is looking pretty good to me. Wrath-Grounding Guard and Lightning Drinking Blade are really campaign dependent. If you're dealing with rebellions or battling mutant armies in your outcaste run fringe kingdom then it's not likely to show up very often. If you're battling other dragonblooded, sorcerers, gods, demons, elementals, and ghosts on a regular basis it's going to be a lot more helpful.<br /> <br /> Even if it's out of aspect it's probably worth picking up Flame Warden Stance as it gives you a lot more freedom, and you can use the fire aura effect of it until you get into Earth aura.<br /> <br /> Spilling the Mountain's Blood is good, but best against really big opponents. Adding overflow successes to damage, then adding another 40% to the damage, and then causing them to suffer a 6L/round difficulty 5 hazard is pretty punchy. You might want to pair it with (Element) Protection Technique though, since there's a good chance you're going to be brawling in a lava pool by the end of your next turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1379470#post1379470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. 5/1/5 Brawler \u2013 mucking around with trying to make this, well, not good but fun to play thanks to Flotsam-and-Jetsam Approach (FYI, basically allows you to use strength with improvised weapons for a scene for 1m). End up just spamming Ox-Bodies at the minute, and realising that Water has so many toys it's hard to justify going with any other aspect, even if I'd like to make an Ragara Earth-aspected brutish debt collector work (although honourable mention for Wood and Oaken Thew Exertion).</div> </div> </div> </div>Earth Brawl is pretty good. Grab these, bold indicates charms that are neither Earth nor Balanced:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Flotsam-and-Jetsam Approach</b><br /> Become the Hammer<br /> Water Dragon's Coils<br /> Inescapable Whirlpool Hold<br /> Crushing Avalanche Grasp<br /> Pounding Surf Style<br /> Stone Fist Strike<br /> Rolling Boulder Blow<br /> Firmament Shattering Impact<br /> <b>Hammering Wave Technique<br /> Fist Spinning Maelstrom</b><br /> At Essence 4 Magma Hell Upheaval<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Floatsam-and-Jetsam can be used reflexively as soon as combat starts, right when you roll join battle so it doesn't mess with your aura. Your withering attacks get enhanced with by the enemy's onslaught penalty and your Essence to your Overwhelming to punch through high soak. Your decisive attacks add (Strength) threshold successes, let you smash an enemy both back and prone literally cratering them and surrounding them with difficult terrain, possibly even throwing them back to Medium or Long range and taking additional fall damage. Your grapples get to use (Strength + Brawl) to hit, add threshold successes to the gambit roll, dissapearing 6s on the gambit roll, and attacks that miss or don't deal damage don't take away control rounds.<br /> <br /> Although Flotsam-and-Jetsam Approach isn't compatible with Stone Fist Strike, so look to use SFS against opponents with soak so high you'll never penetrate it, and smack any other poor bastard with the table leg otherwise.<br /> <br /> You also have the option of holding back from going totemic anima and using Water aura charms, or even doing both and doing things like get into Water Aura to use Fist Spinning Maelstrom to wither everyone around you, and then flare totemic, automatically shifting to Earth aura, and annihilating one enemy with Crater-Making Impact. Later on you can even use Fist Spinning Maelstrom to wither a ton of people and knock them prone, and then use Magma Hell Upheaval to smack all their prone selves with an unblockable magma tidal wave.<br /> <br /> Let me remind you that prone characters have a flat -2 to their Evasion against this unblockable attack.<br /> <br /> There are definitely more toys that a pure water brawler gets to play with, but I'd say Earth still looks good with fun and variation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-08-2020, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T16:08:51-07:00","id":1379540,"title":"","content":"So here's an actual build for Olmar, an immaculate investigator who hunts down heretics and criminals and punctures their armor with his direlance. He either hunts down local criminals or immaculate heretics, but if the case arises that the criminal or heretic in question is a fairy or anathema he won't shy away from it. Secretly though, he wishes he could just master his calligraphy in peace, but he knows his skills and natural talent to violence, combined with the evils of the world force him to put that aside for now.<br /> <br /> As an investigator he's top notch to track down leads, case scenes, profile characters. He's also got stealth for tailing people unnoticed and launching ambushes once he's got his mark made. In combat he's a monster and particularly capable against foes with heavy armor. Even at Essence 2 with Unerring Lightning Razor he's launching a piercing attack with 18 dice to hit, re-rolling four non-1s, then dealing +19 damage, ignoring 4 points of soak, re-rolling four non-1s.<br /> <br /> If he could pair up with an earth aspect that uses Weigh Down Armor to increase an opponent's mobility penalty by 3, or an archer who uses Life Swelling Sap Strike to lower it by 1, that would be even better.<br /> <br /> When he gets to Essence 3 he'll get the air signature Investigation, dodge and melee charms.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 5 Str<br /> 3 Dex<br /> 4 Sta<br /> <br /> 2 Cha<br /> 3 Man<br /> 2 App<br /> <br /> 4 Per<br /> 5 Int<br /> 2 Wits<br /> <br /> <br /> 0 Archery<br /> 3 *Athletics<br /> 3 Awareness<br /> 2 Brawl<br /> 0 Bureaucracy<br /> 0 Craft<br /> 5 *Dodge (Unarmored)<br /> 2 Integrity (Immaculate dogma, suspected criminals/heretics)<br /> 5 *Investigation (Heretical crime)<br /> 0 Larceny<br /> 2 *Linguistics (Calligraphy)<br /> 2 *Lore (Background: Immaculate Training)<br /> 0 Medicine<br /> 5 *Melee<br /> 0 *Occult<br /> 0 Performance<br /> 0 Presence<br /> 3 *Resistance<br /> 0 Ride<br /> 0 Sail<br /> 0 Socialize<br /> 3 *Stealth<br /> 0 Survival<br /> 0 *Thrown<br /> 0 War<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> 4 Backing Immaculate Order<br /> 3 Influence Immaculate Monk<br /> 3 Lightning Dancer (Direlance)<br /> 3 Contacts Immaculate Order Blessed Isle<br /> 1 Language (Low Realm)<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> Free Excellencies<br /> Dodge<br /> Melee<br /> Investigation<br /> Athletics<br /> Stealth<br /> <br /> <br /> 15 Starting Charms<br /> Burning Fury Wreath<br /> Crimson Fang Bite<br /> Flame Born Interception<br /> Oncoming Storm Stance<br /> Unerring Lightning Razor<br /> <br /> Ox-Body Technique<br /> Impervious Skin of Stone<br /> <br /> Permeating Insight<br /> Scent-of-Crime Method<br /> Heart-Maze Navigation<br /> Tampering Detection Technique<br /> Revelation of Associates Hunch<br /> <br /> Frozen Heart Prana<br /> <br /> Vanishing Wind-Body Technique<br /> Soundless Action Prana<br /> <br /> Bonus Point Usage<br /> 4 on Stamina<br /> 4 on Intelligence<br /> 2 on Dodge<br /> 2 on Melee<br /> 2 on Investigation<br /> 1 on language<br /> 1 on Lore<br /> 2 on Willpower<br /> <br /> <br /> Combat stats<br /> Join battle 5<br /> Lightning Dancer 9(+5) (Damage 19/5)<br /> Dodge 5(+3)<br /> Soak 4(+4 for 4m)<br /> <br /> 13/26 motes, 6wp<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T00:18:06-07:00","id":1379683,"title":"","content":"He looks great. I've pretty much never looked at the direlance unless thinking about using ride (not sure why), fun to see a character built to use one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T07:06:21-07:00","id":1379752,"title":"","content":"So, out of interest.<br /> <br /> I'm playing a Wood-Aspect in a high-Essence mixed game (3 Solars, 1 Lunar, 2 DBs, one Raksha). The campaign features a lot of undead, strange monsters, spirits, etc. Very rarely other Exalts. These are my combat charms: anything new (or old) that you think would go really well with them? <u>Archery</u><br /> Excellency, Harvest of the Hunter, Arrow Thorn Technique, Life-Swelling Sap Strike, Heartbeats Before Death<br /> <u>Medicine</u><br /> Excellency, Venom-Expulsion Method, Poisoner's Deft Hand<br /> <u>Resistance</u><br /> Ox-Body Technique x5, Impervious Skin of Stone, Supple Viridian Scales, Element Protection Technique, Well-Tended Garden of the Soul, Dragon's Unfailing Vigour<br /> <u>Ride</u><br /> Tread Rooted in Life (Wood, Earth, Water), Great Heart Companion, Dance of the Jade Bridle<br /> <u>Evocations of Night-Bane</u><br /> Hundred Devils Purgation, Argent Panacea Arrow<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T08:45:20-07:00","id":1379769,"title":"","content":"<i>(Some not especially insightful stuff but hopefully of use...)</i><br /> <br /> Rolling Stormcloud Approach seems the gamechanger for Deeb archery. You can aim on the move, but it's air aura and that might be tough to get into.<br /> <br /> From the Occult tree in WFHW, Dragon's Sacred Talon should be pretty useful for fighting spirts (pg 231) if you've not got it already.<br /> <br /> The two teamwork war charms from Heirs, especially if the other DB in your group is a hearthmate and good in a fight, look nuts. Shared initiative, a free full excellency each, shared auras...<br /> <br /> Maybe less relevant, but something that I'd like to try \u2013 if you're Wood and the beast you're riding is a familiar then Dragon-Beast Transformation in Heirs looks fun. If you're at Essence 5 you could even get yourself a flying familiar and mutate yourself some wings.<br /> <br /> Flying archer DB in the vein of the below (in my head at least)...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wjv7rH3X0yo?t=39\" data-code=\"wjv7rH3X0yo\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/wjv7rH3X0yo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-09-2020, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T10:34:12-07:00","id":1379801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1379769#post1379769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rolling Stormcloud Approach seems the gamechanger for Deeb archery. You can aim on the move, but it's air aura and that might be tough to get into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Air Aura is pretty easy to do Archery in, if you look at the WFHW Charms. Sky Calming Draw, Death From Nowhere, and Drawing Lightning Style are all very spammable. Horizon Spanning Arc is a great capstone ability. Adding in Rolling Stormcloud Approach doesn't look a hassle to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1379769#post1379769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe less relevant, but something that I'd like to try \u2013 if you're Wood and the beast you're riding is a familiar then Dragon-Beast Transformation in Heirs looks fun. If you're at Essence 5 you could even get yourself a flying familiar and mutate yourself some wings.<br /> <br /> Flying archer DB in the vein of the below (in my head at least)...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wjv7rH3X0yo?t=39\" data-code=\"wjv7rH3X0yo\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/wjv7rH3X0yo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>And what do you get until you hit E5?<br /> <br /> Are there any 3-4 dot Mutations which are worth a Charm? I thought this one was kinda lacklustre. Unusual Hide 3 and Unusual Hide 4 are the only options which seem vaguely useful.<br /> <br /> Spending 8XP to gain 9XPs worth of mutations IF I commit 5m all day is a bad trade. 8XP to get 12XP of mutations is still a bad trade, because of those committed motes. <br /> <br /> 8XP to get 15XP Flight for 5m is absolutely rocking, though. No objections there. But at that point this is an Essence 5 Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T11:02:22-07:00","id":1379812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1379801#post1379801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Air Aura is pretty easy to do Archery in, if you look at the WFHW Charms. Sky Calming Draw, Death From Nowhere, and Drawing Lightning Style are all very spammable. Horizon Spanning Arc is a great capstone ability. Adding in Rolling Stormcloud Approach doesn't look a hassle to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>But he doesn't have any of them yet - just the wood archery charms so getting into air aura <i>right now</i> isn't on. Will take a bit of collecting, but yeah, as you say, amazing once you have them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Are there any 3-4 dot Mutations which are worth a Charm? I thought this one was kinda lacklustre. Unusual Hide 3 and Unusual Hide 4 are the only options which seem vaguely useful. </div> </div> </div>You've got me there, although I'm thinking of someone who has a menagerie so you could pick and choose what you get. Centaur to be permantly mounted is probably the obvious one, allowing you to split from your ride and let it do it's thing if it's good in combat on its own - but that's a big if.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's just a save to Essence 5 or the number of mutations get a bump at publication. I had similar thoughts about the summoning elementals charm. But it appeals to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:20:02-07:00","id":1379860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1379801#post1379801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any 3-4 dot Mutations which are worth a Charm? I thought this one was kinda lacklustre. Unusual Hide 3 and Unusual Hide 4 are the only options which seem vaguely useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's just the one familiar probably not, but if you've got a lot of familiars. You can also use it with Dragon's Egg Hatched and Elemental Bond Meditation to just summon up an elemental with the mutations you want at a moment's notice and take them for yourself that way.<br /> <br /> An archer going into a place where you need to conceal your weapons? Natural missile. Want to exploit some water feature, or just need to spend a lot of time under water? Gills. Imposing features lets you penalize an enemy's Resolve by 1 in order to create a tie for you. Smokescreen lets you blind enemies that you disengage from, which can be a huge help combined with allies since it only affects enemies.<br /> <br /> If you want Mighty Thews on demand that could be good, or Danger Sense, or Fast Reflexes. Spinnerets could be really fun too. Centaur gives you all the benefits of being mounted even when you're not, so that's +1 non-charm defense, plus bonus damage and the ability to make impaling attacks. There's some other good ones there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:42:16-07:00","id":1379903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1379860#post1379860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's just the one familiar probably not, but if you've got a lot of familiars. You can also use it with <b>Dragon's Egg Hatched</b> and Elemental Bond Meditation to just summon up an elemental with the mutations you want at a moment's notice and take them for yourself that way.<br /> <br /> An archer going into a place where you need to conceal your weapons? Natural missile. Want to exploit some water feature, or just need to spend a lot of time under water? Gills. Imposing features lets you penalize an enemy's Resolve by 1 in order to create a tie for you. Smokescreen lets you blind enemies that you disengage from, which can be a huge help combined with allies since it only affects enemies.<br /> <br /> If you want Mighty Thews on demand that could be good, or Danger Sense, or Fast Reflexes. Spinnerets could be really fun too. Centaur gives you all the benefits of being mounted even when you're not, so that's +1 non-charm defense, plus bonus damage and the ability to make impaling attacks. There's some other good ones there.</div> </div> </div> </div><s>Yes, at Essence 5 this Charm is good. I've already conceded that.<br /> <br /> Otherwise who has a menagerie of Familiars?<br /> <br /> You get the abilities your Familiar already has. So yes, you can go Centuar... or you could just ride your horse Familiar. Yes, you can impose -1 Resolve if creating a Tie towards you (keep in mind the Charms which automatically create a Tie), but until Essence 5 you can't swap that out for Gills or Natural Missile or Smokescreen... because it's one power set per Familiar and you don't have multiple Familiars.<br /> <br /> You get one power based on your one Familiar until you hit Essence 5. At which point you get Wings (or Unnatural Hide 6).<br /> <br /> I guess Elemental Bond Meditation and Sorcery could let you create three Elemental Familiars. I don't know. I still don't feel it. Seems like a big investment.</s><br /> <br /> Got the Essence requirements wrong. Yeah, no objections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-10-2020, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:26:06-07:00","id":1379925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1379903#post1379903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, at Essence 5 this Charm is good. I've already conceded that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon's Egg Hatched is an Essence 3 charm...?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1379903#post1379903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise who has a menagerie of Familiars?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the pre-req charms for Dragon-Beast Transformation lets you take on animals as familiars for no experience cost. So if you start out as Essence 1-2 Dragonblooded you can use your time to be one with nature and spend a week or two here and there getting at least four or five animals. They don't have to be big impressive things, Gills can come from any aquatic or amphibious creature, Burrower can come from a gopher. If you grab 3-4 of them you're probably looking at enough to make the charm worthwhile.<br /> <br /> It won't be one of the best survival charms that DBs have access to, but not every new charm needs to be better than all the other ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1379903#post1379903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you can impose -1 Resolve if creating a Tie towards you (keep in mind the Charms which automatically create a Tie</div> </div> </div> </div>How many charms automatically create a tie without needing to overcome resolve? Dragon Warlord's Convocation doesn't even do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1379903#post1379903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get one power based on your one Familiar until you hit Essence 5. At which point you get Wings (or Unnatural Hide 6).</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically it's dots of mutations, so you can have Smokescreen and Fins from your cuttlefish familiar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:50:02-07:00","id":1379936,"title":"","content":"If I were trying to make DB Lois Lane, Intrepid Reporter... any goodies for that build in Heirs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:17:22-07:00","id":1379955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1379936#post1379936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were trying to make DB Lois Lane, Intrepid Reporter... any goodies for that build in Heirs?</div> </div> </div> </div>A charm that lets you much more easily profile or read the intentions of a fairies and other Wyld creatures, as well as case the scenes they were involved in, or even just Wyld energy. One that lets you read the intentions and break encryption of other terrestrials better, it also lets you communicate with them across language barriers. One that lets you raise your vision to a point in the sky and see everything from above.<br /> <br /> The bureacracy ones are pretty good. One lets you instantly spot what kind of bureaucratic standing in what kind of bureaucratic organization a character has. Like spotting a member of the Deliberative out in the street, or picking out an important guild factor. One that lets you introduce facts about any kind of bureaucracy, even if you're not familiar with it, as long as you've investigated it for a scene.<br /> <br /> One coming off of the Doctor Who psychic paper charm lets you convince people that you not only belong where you are, but are in a position of authority there.<br /> <br /> A resistance charm that lets you store your armor in an elemental expression also lets you form exceptional clothing out of it, which also gains benefits for the element like water adding to disguises or air adding to stealth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T01:04:13-07:00","id":1380051,"title":"","content":"&gt;Dragon Egg Hatched is Essence 3<br /> <br /> Whoops! So it is. Yeah, that's pretty good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T03:44:33-07:00","id":1380071,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s a character build that I\u2019m hoping to use as an antagonist that (a) shows off some of the new Earth melee and (b) is easy enough to run (i.e. doesn\u2019t worry much about aura). Idea is he\u2019s an honourable, unstoppable legion officer who has been called back as the Great Houses shape up for war and essentially earmarked by the house\u2019s powers that be as the enforcer for his geomancer/demonologist prodigy cousin (who\u2019s a drug-addicted loose cannon) who has been tasked with furthering Ragara\u2019s research into the <i>bad stuff</i>. He\u2019s not happy about it \u2013 which way is his loyalty going to go?<br /> <br /> Supposed to be re<span style=\"font-family:arial\">lati</span>vely balanced (if five Ox-Bodies and Pain Tolerance can be called that, but he\u2019s intended to reoccur so being tough to kill seems to make sense). Min-maxing would involve dropping intelligence and stamina to 1, dropping Impervious Skin of Stone till you\u2019ve upped stamina and ditching some of the fluff dots, buying more favoured abilities and merits instead, taking one of the named Grand Goremauls with free evocations etc etc (if that suits your game).<br /> <br /> If he was being played I\u2019d look to grab things like Dragon-Graced Weapon and definitely Falling Mountain Fang to carry on the theme \u2013 his cousin uses Elemental Bolt Attack so Wrath-Grounding Guard might come into play in the event of a falling out \u2013 it\u2019s situational otherwise so not bought here yet. He\u2019s pretty immobile so looking at ranged/mobility options would be high up the priority list.<br /> <br /> To figure out how viable Earth melee is I ran a fight with him against, well, Volfer. Didn\u2019t want to disrupt the epic fight/discussion going on in the Arena thread at the minute, so chucked it here behind spoilers along with some thoughts on how it worked out.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Chargen Earth Aspected Melee Dynast</u></b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> House of Bells<br /> <br /> ATTRIBUTES (8 BP used here)<br /> <br /> 5 Strength<br /> 5 Dexterity<br /> 3 Stamina<br /> <br /> 1 Charisma<br /> 2 Manipulation<br /> 4 Appearance<br /> <br /> 3 Perception<br /> 2 Intelligence<br /> 4 Wits<br /> <br /> ABILITIES (8 BP used here)<br /> <br /> Aspect<br /> <br /> Awareness 5 (Join Battle)<br /> Craft 0<br /> Integrity 2<br /> Resistance 5<br /> War 3 (Exploiting Terrain)<br /> <br /> Favoured<br /> <br /> Lore 1<br /> Occult 1<br /> Thrown 1 (Javelins)<br /> Athletics 5 (Rushes)<br /> Melee 5 (Tetsubo)<br /> <br /> Other<br /> <br /> Linguistics 1<br /> Dodge 3<br /> Socialise 3<br /> Brawl 1<br /> <br /> MERITS (2 BP used here)<br /> <br /> (Native Language: High Realm)<br /> <br /> Artefact 3 (Grand Goremaul)<br /> Artefact 3 (Reinforced Breastplate)<br /> Pain Tolerance 4<br /> Resources 3<br /> Backing 3 (House Ragara)<br /> Hearthstone 2 (Stone of the Ram\u2019s Horn)<br /> Language 1 (Low Realm)<br /> Language 1 (Riverspeak)<br /> <br /> CHARMS<br /> <br /> Free Excellencies<br /> <br /> Athletics<br /> Awareness<br /> Integrity<br /> Melee<br /> War<br /> <br /> 1. Ox-Body Technique<br /> 2. Ox-Body Technique<br /> 3. Ox-Body Technique<br /> 4. Ox-Body Technique<br /> 5. Ox-Body Technique<br /> 6. Resistance: Impervious Skin of Stone<br /> 7. Melee: Flame-Born Interception<br /> 8. Melee: Blinding Spark Distraction<br /> 9. Melee: Crossfire Flash<br /> 10. Melee: Dragon-Scale Shield<br /> 11. Melee: Rumbling Earth Rebuke<br /> 12. Awareness: Deep-Listening Palm<br /> 13. Awareness: All-Encompassing Earth Sense<br /> 14. Awareness: Pasiap Preempts Haste<br /> 15. War: Roaring Dragon Officer<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>EDIT: Initiative screw-up on turn 3 fixed. Apologies.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Fight</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Starts at medium range</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">One-point stunts assumed</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Join Battle</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Earth Aspect rolls 12 dice + 3 successes (6m Excellency) + willpower + Pasiap Preempts Haste (3m) for 11i. Anima at glowing.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Volfer rolls 16 dice (6m Excellency) + willpower for 9i</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">TURN 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>EA: 11i (13p/11ph, 4 WP, 1a)</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Volfer: 9i (13p/27ph, 5 WP)</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">EA delays turn (-0i because of Pasiap Preempts Haste)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Volfer closes to short and uses Thunderclap Rush (3m) to launch a withering attack using Excellent Strike (3m), Fire and Stones Strike (5m), Excellency (6m) and willpower for 18 dice + 2 successes.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">EA boosts his parry to 12 with Dragon-Scale Shield (1m, 1i, +1 non-charm to parry when used with a heavy weapon), a full Excellency (6m) and willpower. Anima at burning.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Volfer gets 11 successes, attack misses.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">EA makes a withering smashing attack (-1i) using a 3m Excellency, the Pasiap Preempts Haste bonus (3 dice) and willpower for 20 dice + 1 success.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Volfer defends with full Excellency (8m), Durability of Oak (3m) and willpower for a parry of 11.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">EA gets 11 successes, attack hits. Damage pool of 19 (5 Strength + 14 Weapon Damage), Volfer uses Spirit Strengthens the Skin (4m) to boost his soak to effectively 13 (including the Durability of Oak bonus).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">6 dice of damage gives two successes. Volfer is prone.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">EA enters earth aura.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">TURN 2:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Mote regen</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>EA: 12i (13p/6ph, 2 WP, 2a)</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Volfer: 7i (8p/5ph, 3 WP, prone)</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">EA makes a withering attack using a full Excellency (5m) for 20 dice. Volfer defends with Excellency (2m), Durability of Oak and willpower for a parry of 6 after onslaught and being knocked prone. Anima at bonfire.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">EA gets 9 successes, attack hits. Damage pool of 22. Volfer repeats his use of Spirit Strengthens the Skin (4m) to boost his soak to 13. 9 dice of damage gives four successes.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">EA: 17i (13p/1ph, 2 WP, 3a)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Volfer: 3i (4p/0ph, 2 WP, prone)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Volfer flurries rise from prone, spending 1 willpower to make sure he makes it, with an unenhanced withering attack, rolling 9 dice after the flurry penalty.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">EA\u2019s parry is 7. Volfer gets 9 successes, attack hits.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Damage pool is 15. At bonfire, EA soak is at 17, so Volfer is reduced to overwhelming damage. 1 dice gives no successes.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">TURN 3:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Mote regen</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Anima flux does nothing</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>EA: 17i (13p/6ph, 2 WP, 3a)</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Volfer: 4i (4p/5ph, 1 WP)</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">EA delays to clash (drops to 15i).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Volfer goes all out with a withering attack using Excellent Strike, 6m Excellency and willpower for 18 dice + 2 successes.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">EA clashes with a withering smashing attack (-1i) using full Excellency (6m), Crossfire Flash (5m) and willpower for 22 dice + 1 success.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Volfer gets 10 successes, EA gets 12 success after Crossfire Flash re-rolls.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Damage pool is 21, resulting in 14 dice damage and 4 successes. Volfer is knocked prone and crashed.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>EA: 27i (8p/0ph, 1 WP, 3a)</i><br /> <i>Volfer: 0i (0p/0ph, 0 WP, prone)</i><br /> <br /> EA activates Rumbling Earth Rebuke (4m, 1wp), triggering a reflexive disarm gambit. Volfer\u2019s parry is 2 (-1 prone, -2 from losing a clash).<br /> <br /> EA rolls 11 dice for 5 successes. Attack hits, and he passes the initiative roll easily (-4i). Volfer\u2019s chopping sword is destroyed.<br /> <br /> TURN 4:<br /> <i>Mote regen</i><br /> <i>Anima flux does nothing</i><br /> <i>EA: 23i (4p/5ph, 0 WP, 3a)</i><br /> <i>Volfer: 0i (0p/5ph, 0 WP, prone)</i><br /> <br /> EA makes a withering attack using a full Excellency (5m) for 20 dice. Volfer\u2019s parry is now at 0 (Brawl parry of 4, -1 prone, -2 from losing a clash, -1 from Rumbling Earth Rebuke in Earth aura). He stunts and uses a 4m Excellency to reach parry 3.<br /> <br /> EA gets 9 successes, attack hits, damage pool of 25. 18 dice give 4 successes (yet AGAIN).<br /> <br /> EA: 28i (4p/0ph, 0 WP, 3a)<br /> Volfer: -4i (0p/1ph, 0 WP, prone)<br /> <br /> Volfer flurries rise from prone with a withering brawl attack. He makes the rise from prone and rolls 10 dice. EA uses a 1m Excellency and Blinding Spark Distraction (1m, 1i) for a parry of 8. Volfer rolls 3 successes, misses and is blinded.<br /> <br /> TURN 5:<br /> <i>Mote regen</i><br /> <i>Anima flux inflicts 1 HL and knocks Volfer prone</i><br /> <i>EA: 25i (2p/5ph, 0 WP, 3a)</i><br /> <i>Volfer: -4i (0p/6ph, 0 WP, blinded, prone)</i><br /> <br /> EA makes a decisive attack using a full Excellency (4m) for 19 dice.<br /> <br /> Volfer uses 6m Excellency to boost his parry to 4 (Parry of 4 + 3 Excellency + 1 Stunt \u2013 1 prone \u2013 3 blinded). 6 successes, attack hits.<br /> <br /> 25 initiative give 13 successes, Volfer is down.</span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Notes <i>(AKA much too long random witterings)</i></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">- I may have screwed up here in turn 2 on the melee excellency when Volfer hit \u2013 if I don\u2019t use the charm (having already used it that turn) but fail to parry does that attack count in terms of resetting the discount?<br /> <br /> - Dragon-Scale Shield giving heavy weapons a boost was the difference in turn 1. Think Earth's version is my favourite.<br /> <br /> - Rumbling Earth Rebuke worked here and is powerful if held back for when motes are low, but obviously situational \u2013 Dragon-Graced Weapon or Call the Blade make it an inconvenience. Still, not having to give up an attack but still being able to use a disarm and turn your typical white room Melee 5, Dex 5 nightmare sword fighter into a Dex 5, Brawl 0 target is nice. Perversely, Volfer, as non-optimised as he is, actually has some brawl and was only knocked back a couple of pegs in effectiveness. I \u2018declared\u2019 Rumbling Earth Rebuke in the initial attack \u2013 I probably need to clarify if that\u2019s necessary with devs.<br /> <br /> - Speaking of white rooms, one-on-one duels in particular, I think DB melee probably does \u2018better\u2019 in these than it would in an actual game with extras, battle groups, archers or the like \u2013 the excellency discount and the clash enhancing charms thrive in this environment.<br /> <br /> - I really like Pasiap Preempts Haste \u2013 charms that help you do two things (win JB <i>and</i> improve your first attack) are okay with me.<br /> <br /> - I\u2019ve thought this before, but earth\u2019s anima power seems OP to me. Leaving aside the soak, being able to knock people prone is a most massive debuff, no?<br /> <br /> - Benchmarking builds against Volfer <i>(nothing original here so feel free to ignore)</i> \u2013 as has been noted elsewhere he doesn\u2019t have all his charms/merits etc so I should probably not do that any more as that way lies non-fun \u2018If you can\u2019t beat Volfer are you <i>even</i> Exalted?\u2019 thinking. Also, while this fight was straightforward, as maligned as he is as a Dawn, Volfer has a good shot at landing that opening attack on a pretty-near optimised DB and then going into a One Weapon, Two Blows combo to suck defensive motes and potentially inflict a wound penalty. The clash could have gone his way too with a little luck. Still think the DB would win if either of those had happened, he has too many health levels and artefacts, but Volfer\u2019s not <i>that </i>bad \u2013 y\u2019know, like Scroll of Exalts Solars bad. He\u2019s incomplete.<br /> <br /> - Urgh. Really should just type these out in full as I go rather than cobble notes together afterwards.</span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-10-2020, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T03:59:20-07:00","id":1380072,"title":"","content":"You should definitely cross post thisto the Arena.<br /> <br /> The signature characters (and Isthus) are built like you are SUPPOSED to build your character. Volfer isn't at full power, but he's built along the lines of what should be typical. I'd switch to using Isthus as my benchmark character, but he plays awkwardly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T03:59:22-07:00","id":1380073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1379752#post1379752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, out of interest.<br /> <br /> I'm playing a Wood-Aspect in a high-Essence mixed game (3 Solars, 1 Lunar, 2 DBs, one Raksha). The campaign features a lot of undead, strange monsters, spirits, etc. Very rarely other Exalts. These are my combat charms: anything new (or old) that you think would go really well with them? <u>Archery</u><br /> Excellency, Harvest of the Hunter, Arrow Thorn Technique, Life-Swelling Sap Strike, Heartbeats Before Death<br /> <u>Medicine</u><br /> Excellency, Venom-Expulsion Method, Poisoner's Deft Hand<br /> <u>Resistance</u><br /> Ox-Body Technique x5, Impervious Skin of Stone, Supple Viridian Scales, Element Protection Technique, Well-Tended Garden of the Soul, Dragon's Unfailing Vigour<br /> <u>Ride</u><br /> Tread Rooted in Life (Wood, Earth, Water), Great Heart Companion, Dance of the Jade Bridle<br /> <u>Evocations of Night-Bane</u><br /> Hundred Devils Purgation, Argent Panacea Arrow</div> </div> </div> </div>Looked at Heirs again last night, if you're looking to use stuff from that, short of air archery/Rolling Stormcloud, for that character I'd probably focus on Nightshade's Deadly Bloom. At Essence 3 (after a repurchase), you could create poisonous difficult terrain, which kind of does a similar thing in that it slows your opponents down, hopefully buying you more shots. Not especially insightful, but it's what I'd likely do first up looking at the above.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T04:14:27-07:00","id":1380075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1379936#post1379936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were trying to make DB Lois Lane, Intrepid Reporter... any goodies for that build in Heirs?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1379955#post1379955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A charm that lets you much more easily profile or read the intentions of a fairies and other Wyld creatures, as well as case the scenes they were involved in, or even just Wyld energy. One that lets you read the intentions and break encryption of other terrestrials better, it also lets you communicate with them across language barriers. One that lets you raise your vision to a point in the sky and see everything from above.<br /> <br /> The bureacracy ones are pretty good. One lets you instantly spot what kind of bureaucratic standing in what kind of bureaucratic organization a character has. Like spotting a member of the Deliberative out in the street, or picking out an important guild factor. One that lets you introduce facts about any kind of bureaucracy, even if you're not familiar with it, as long as you've investigated it for a scene.<br /> <br /> One coming off of the Doctor Who psychic paper charm lets you convince people that you not only belong where you are, but are in a position of authority there.<br /> <br /> A resistance charm that lets you store your armor in an elemental expression also lets you form exceptional clothing out of it, which also gains benefits for the element like water adding to disguises or air adding to stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd add, given it's Lois Lane and she has a black belt in getting into trouble, Heart Conquering Prowess in presence might be good, a balanced fire charm that adds appearance/2 to your attack roll and lets you instill ties. It plays like the trope where the nosey reporter is being intimidated by the mob boss and she puts him on his ass, earning his respect.<br /> <br /> There's a seduction one too in presence, if you're the type of reporter/game to use a honeypot scheme, plus two good socialise ones \u2013 one that makes you always look clean/dapper ('how does she manage to look that good in the middle of a war zone?') and lowers the cost of lots of other social charms, and one that enhances any disguise you've put together to sneak into where you shouldn't be ('yes, that is my name tag, I was having a bad hair day').","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T08:33:44-07:00","id":1403236,"title":"","content":"Shrugging Water Dragon Escape<br /> Drowning-in-Blood Technique<br /> Flowing Water Defense<br /> Water Dragon Form<br /> <br /> Blinding Spark Throw<br /> Venomous Thorn Attack<br /> <br /> Seed and Salt Warding<br /> Spirit-Grounding Shout<br /> Secret Wind Revelation<br /> Spirit-Detecting Mirror Technique<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery Invulnerable Skin of Bronze Mists of Eventide<br /> <br /> Ox-Body Technique<br /> <br /> Frozen Heart Prana<br /> Slippery Thoughts Technique<br /> <br /> Frost-Thorn Knuckle 3<br /> Kaijin 3 <br /> <br /> 20+ soak can attack against spirits 7+ parry","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T10:43:48-07:00","id":1403546,"title":"","content":"Idea I had recently that at least tangentially fits in this thread:<br /> <br /> Willpower costs getting you down? Make sure at least a couple of your Intimacies are sufficiently ripe for suffering hardship on account of. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T01:47:35-07:00","id":1419744,"title":"","content":"<i>(Pops Thread Necromancy Technique)</i><br /> <br /> So my character died last session (act of self-sacrifice during one of the most fun sessions I've ever had). I'm idly musing ideas for a new one, with the minor proviso that, despite a distinct lack of talent for it, I seem to be ST-ing more and more so this person will primarily be a plot mouthpiece/support character.<br /> <br /> Anyone got any fun/slightly off the wall ability/aspect mash-ups they've always been curious to try out?<br /> <br /> My last character was Wood and big on Performance, Swaying Grass Dance style and Medicine, thinking of going for something a bit more off the beaten track. I\u2019m fine for dreaming up actual concepts/characteristics (narrowing it down is usually more the problem\u2026), more looking for stuff that\u2019s mechanically interesting to refine right now.<br /> <br /> We've got an Earth magistrate who focuses on Melee/Resistance/Investigation/Awareness, their wandering Immaculate Earth Aspect sibling who uses Earth Dragon and is beginning to get into Craft, and a Fire sorcerer. Our game has been Blessed Isle/Investigation into Ragara shenanigans heavy thus far, but will probably broaden in scope from here as we build to the Civil War.<br /> <br /> First thought was exploring the support angle, looking at the Lore tutoring tree, Victory-Seeking Insight and Tiger-and-Dragon Combination. Anything anyone cares to share is most welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T02:20:17-07:00","id":1419746,"title":"","content":"(Side note: I'd quite like to avoid rolling or \u2013 more accurately \u2013 forgetting to roll poison/resistance for quite some time, thank you very much...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T06:41:52-07:00","id":1419781,"title":"","content":"What Essence are you looking at?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T06:52:43-07:00","id":1419782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1419781#post1419781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Essence are you looking at?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tempted to just go back to basics at E2 to keep things simple as I'm really not worried about being overshadowed or the like, but group consensus is going in where everyone else is \u2013 low E3, 90 EXP or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T07:28:54-07:00","id":1419783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1419782#post1419782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\